---
title: "What happens when I enter dhwanijain.me and press Enter (Railway, then what changes on Azure)"
---
sequenceDiagram
  participant L as Laptop<br/>browser + OS<br/>Wi-Fi card
  participant H as Home network<br/>access point · switch<br/>router · modem
  participant I as ISP +<br/>internet routers
  participant D as DNS<br/>resolver → root →<br/>.me → Cloudflare
  participant E as Railway edge<br/>public IP<br/>:80 and :443
  participant A as App container<br/>Uvicorn, 2 workers<br/>on $PORT
  participant P as PostgreSQL<br/>:5432, private
  participant G as Google<br/>Analytics

  rect rgb(245, 245, 245)
    Note over L,G: STEP 1 · START IN THE BROWSER
    Note over L: Parse the URL<br/>scheme http · host dhwanijain.me<br/>port 80 · path /<br/>Assume: no cached DNS answer
    Note over L,I: DHCP already gave the laptop: private IP, subnet mask,<br/>default gateway (the router), DNS server
  end

  rect rgb(232, 240, 255)
    Note over L,G: STEP 2 · DNS LOOKUP · separate from the web request · client: laptop, server: resolver
    L->>D: What is the IP of dhwanijain.me? (UDP 53)
    Note over D: Resolver asks root → .me → Cloudflare<br/>Cloudflare flattens the CNAME to Railway's A records
    D-->>L: Railway edge IP address
  end

  rect rgb(255, 244, 224)
    Note over L,G: STEP 3 · CONNECT · client: laptop, server: Railway edge
    Note over L,D: Every packet from here on crosses: Wi-Fi → access point → switch → router → modem → ISP → internet routers<br/>Router NAT: private source IP → public IP, maps replies back<br/>Stateful firewall lets the replies back in
    L->>E: HTTP GET / on port 80
    E-->>L: 301 redirect to https://dhwanijain.me/ (assumed, unverified)
    L->>E: TCP handshake on port 443 (SYN, SYN-ACK, ACK)
    L->>E: TLS hello, SNI = dhwanijain.me
    E-->>L: Certificate
    Note over L: Check name, dates, chain<br/>then agree on session keys
  end

  rect rgb(232, 248, 236)
    Note over L,G: STEP 4 · THE REQUEST REACHES MY APP
    L->>E: GET / · Host: dhwanijain.me (encrypted)
    Note over E: TLS ENDS HERE
    E->>A: Plain HTTP on $PORT (private) · client: edge, server: Uvicorn
    A->>P: SQL query over private DATABASE_URL · client: app, server: Postgres
    P-->>A: Profile and project rows
    Note over A: FastAPI + Jinja render the HTML
  end

  rect rgb(250, 236, 246)
    Note over L,G: STEP 5 · RESPONSE AND FURTHER REQUESTS
    A-->>E: HTML
    E-->>L: 200 + HTML (encrypted again, router maps it back to my laptop)
    L->>E: GET /static/css/styles.css (same connection)
    L->>G: gtag.js, then a page_view hit (new DNS lookup, TCP, TLS)
  end

  rect rgb(235, 235, 235)
    Note over L,G: WHAT CHANGES ON AZURE · same five steps, different DNS answer and different server side
    Note over D,P: DNS answer: A record 4.155.216.147 (not a flattened CNAME)<br/>NSG firewall allows 80 and 443 → public IP maps to VM private IP 172.16.0.4<br/>Nginx :443 with a Certbot certificate · TLS ENDS AT NGINX<br/>Nginx → Uvicorn on 127.0.0.1:8000 (loopback) → SQLite file on the same disk
  end
